<p>UK police arrested Peter Mandelson, a former British ambassador to the United States and long-time Labour Party figure, on suspicion of “misconduct in public office” as investigators examine his past contacts with the late financier Jeffrey Epstein. The Metropolitan Police said officers detained a 72-year-old man at an address in Camden, London, for questioning; multiple outlets identified the suspect as Mandelson. Investigators are examining allegations—raised in reporting tied to newly released “Epstein files” from the U.S.—that Mandelson improperly shared confidential U.K. government information with Epstein while he was in public office. Police later released Mandelson on bail as the investigation continues, and none of the coverage provided reported charges being filed.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mD8EJayI3SMl06NViS03qFr5Qtb028ILNtHo0rdYuhsErGHZtc7s7WQ0VFLL2A7QgVgD5dUr5LdG6T5UYHlgdiNzM56NB3yVGUmElDBVnSohcWZqdlchTxDMnrZ1Bx8XxTw3S-ZNAf2paciPUdBAjJQqPrm-qAN9x7fhy7DlrxAJRVi18Bins6YBeVopSJHEUgjjaO0pKn9HYEqMX8FlapWRQ4TNhH1_x7yY4xnnPSnWPQ1uX9jFk0qYZ8uIwiWjPMbq3co3YazGsIzK-w' alt='Former British Ambassador to the U.S. Peter Mandelson enters a vehicle in London on February 14, 2026, after a misconduct in public office investigation linked to Jeffrey Epstein files.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Search warrants: Police said the arrest followed search warrants carried out at two addresses in the Wiltshire and Camden areas.</li><li>How the case was triggered: Reports say police opened the criminal investigation earlier this month after the government passed communications involving Mandelson and Epstein to investigators.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Metropolitan Police (London): Police said officers arrested a 72-year-old man at an address in Camden on suspicion of misconduct in public office and took him to a London police station for questioning. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/uk-ex-ambassador-mandelson-released-on-bail-in-epstein-probe/a-7